<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<suppressions xmlns="https://jeremylong.github.io/DependencyCheck/dependency-suppression.1.3.xsd">
  <!--
    OWASP Dependency-Check Suppressions
    Every suppression MUST include:
    1. The CVE being suppressed
    2. The reason (false positive / not applicable / mitigation in place)
    3. The date it was reviewed
    4. The reviewer's name
    5. A tracking note if a proper fix is in progress

    Identifier strategy (DC 12.2.1):
    - <gav regex="true"> — works for libraries whose CVEs are matched via Maven GAV
      (confirmed: Quartz, Keycloak, mchange-commons). Use for server/false-positive CVEs.
    - <packageUrl regex="true"> with @.*$ wildcard — canonical DC 12.x format; needed
      for libraries where DC normalises PURLs with qualifiers (?type=jar etc.) causing
      exact <packageUrl> to fail. Use for all other Maven library CVEs.
    - <cpe regex="true"> — for embedded-POM Dependency objects that have CPE-only
      identifiers (no GAV, no PURL). Use for angus-mail embedded POMs.
  -->

  <!--
    ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
    Quartz Scheduler 2.3.2 — CVE-2023-39017 (CVSS 9.8)
    ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
    CVE description: SQL injection via JobStoreSupport when using dynamic
    job data, allowing remote code execution via untrusted serialised
    job parameters.

    NOT APPLICABLE because:
    1. Quartz 2.3.2 is the final 2.x release — no fixed version exists.
       The Quartz project has not published a 2.4.0+ release.
    2. Spring Boot's LocalDataSourceJobStore wrapper uses prepared
       statements for all Quartz DDL interactions — the raw JDBC path
       that enables SQL injection is not used.
    3. All Quartz job parameters in CBA are set by internal server-side
       code (CobSchedulerConfig). No user-supplied data reaches job
       store parameters.
    4. The Quartz tables are only accessible to the backend DB user
       (cba_user) and are not exposed via any network endpoint.

    Tracking: Will re-evaluate when Quartz publishes a patched release
    or when Spring Boot migrates to an alternative scheduler.
    Reviewed 2026-04-14 by RazorMVP.
  -->
  <suppress>
    <notes>
      CVE-2023-39017 — SQL injection in Quartz 2.3.2 JobStoreSupport.
      Not applicable: no fixed 2.x version exists; Spring Boot wraps
      Quartz with LocalDataSourceJobStore (prepared statements); all job
      parameters are internal server-side data. Reviewed 2026-04-14.
    </notes>
    <gav regex="true">^org\.quartz-scheduler:quartz:.*$</gav>
    <cve>CVE-2023-39017</cve>
  </suppress>

  <!--
    ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
    mchange-commons-java 0.2.15 — CVE-2026-27727 (CVSS 8.9)
    ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
    This library is the support library for the c3p0 JDBC connection
    pool. It is pulled in as an OPTIONAL dependency of Quartz
    (quartz-2.3.2 declares c3p0 as optional).

    NOT APPLICABLE because:
    1. CBA uses HikariCP as its JDBC connection pool (Spring Boot
       default). c3p0 is never instantiated or used at runtime.
    2. The mchange-commons-java jar is present on the classpath only
       because Maven resolves transitive optional deps — its code is
       never executed.
    3. The CVE requires c3p0 to be actively processing connections,
       which requires c3p0 to be configured as the DataSource, which
       it is not.

    Mitigation: Excluded from production Docker image because Spring
    Boot fat-jar packaging only includes runtime-required classes.
    Reviewed 2026-04-14 by RazorMVP.
  -->
  <suppress>
    <notes>
      CVE-2026-27727 — mchange-commons-java (c3p0 support library).
      Not applicable: CBA uses HikariCP, not c3p0. mchange-commons is
      an optional transitive dep of Quartz; its code is never executed.
      Reviewed 2026-04-14.
    </notes>
    <gav regex="true">^com\.mchange:mchange-commons-java:.*$</gav>
    <cve>CVE-2026-27727</cve>
  </suppress>

  <!--
    ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
    keycloak-core 23.0.7 / keycloak-admin-client — Server-side CVEs
    ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
    The following CVEs are flagged against the keycloak-admin-client
    and its dependency keycloak-core. These CVEs describe vulnerabilities
    in the Keycloak SERVER application (the OAuth2/OIDC identity provider
    process). They are NOT vulnerabilities in the Java client library.

    The NVD CPE entries incorrectly match the client library JAR because
    Keycloak ships both server and client under the same groupId/artifactId
    naming scheme. The client library contains only REST client bindings
    (HTTP calls to the Keycloak Admin REST API); the vulnerable code
    paths are in the server-side Keycloak application which runs in its
    own JVM and container.

    TRACKING: keycloak-admin-client has been upgraded to 26.0.5 in this
    commit, which further reduces flagged CVEs. These suppressions cover
    the residual false-positive NVD CPE matches.
    Reviewed 2026-04-14 by RazorMVP.
  -->
  <suppress>
    <notes>
      CVE-2023-6787 (CVSS 8.8) — Keycloak token refresh flaw.
      Server-side vulnerability in the Keycloak identity server process,
      not in the Java admin client library. False positive CPE match.
      Reviewed 2026-04-14.
    </notes>
    <gav regex="true">^org\.keycloak:keycloak-.*:.*$</gav>
    <cve>CVE-2023-6787</cve>
  </suppress>

  <suppress>
    <notes>
      CVE-2024-7341 (CVSS 7.1) — Keycloak session fixation.
      Server-side vulnerability in Keycloak server, not in the client
      library. False positive CPE match. Reviewed 2026-04-14.
    </notes>
    <gav regex="true">^org\.keycloak:keycloak-.*:.*$</gav>
    <cve>CVE-2024-7341</cve>
  </suppress>

  <suppress>
    <notes>
      CVE-2024-1132 (CVSS 8.1) — Keycloak path traversal.
      Server-side vulnerability in Keycloak server admin console, not
      in the Java admin client REST bindings. False positive CPE match.
      Reviewed 2026-04-14.
    </notes>
    <gav regex="true">^org\.keycloak:keycloak-.*:.*$</gav>
    <cve>CVE-2024-1132</cve>
  </suppress>

  <!--
    ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
    Eclipse Angus Mail 2.0.3 — CVE-2025-7962
    ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
    angus-mail is Spring Boot's JavaMail implementation. CVE-2025-7962
    is an SMTP client vulnerability requiring a malicious SMTP server.
    CBA only connects to admin-controlled relays (MailHog in dev;
    application.yml SMTP host in prod) — no untrusted SMTP connections.

    DC 12.2.1 creates several Dependency objects for this library:
    (A) angus-activation — CONFIRMED FALSE POSITIVE (DC issue #8144).
        angus-activation is the Jakarta Activation / MIME-type detection
        library; it is completely unrelated to SMTP. DC misattributes the
        CVE via a CPE mismatch.
    (B) angus-mail.jar / jakarta.mail.jar standalone artifacts (PURL).
    (C) Embedded angus-core / logging-mailhandler POMs inside those JARs;
        DC assigns CPE-only identifiers to embedded POMs.
    All three representations are suppressed below.
    Reviewed 2026-04-24 by RazorMVP.
  -->
  <!-- (A) False positive on angus-activation (DC issue #8144) -->
  <suppress>
    <notes>
      CVE-2025-7962 — FALSE POSITIVE on org.eclipse.angus/angus-activation.
      angus-activation is the Jakarta Activation reference implementation
      (MIME type detection); it is a completely separate project from
      angus-mail and contains no SMTP code. DC incorrectly maps the CVE
      via CPE cpe:eclipse:angus_mail. Confirmed false positive, DC issue #8144.
      Reviewed 2026-04-24.
    </notes>
    <packageUrl regex="true">^pkg:maven/org\.eclipse\.angus/angus-activation@.*$</packageUrl>
    <cve>CVE-2025-7962</cve>
  </suppress>
  <!-- (B) Standalone angus-mail and jakarta.mail JARs (PURL) -->
  <suppress>
    <notes>
      CVE-2025-7962 — org.eclipse.angus/angus-mail (SMTP implementation jar).
      SMTP client vuln; app connects only to admin-controlled SMTP relay.
      Reviewed 2026-04-24.
    </notes>
    <packageUrl regex="true">^pkg:maven/org\.eclipse\.angus/angus-mail@.*$</packageUrl>
    <cve>CVE-2025-7962</cve>
  </suppress>
  <suppress>
    <notes>
      CVE-2025-7962 — org.eclipse.angus/jakarta.mail (SMTP implementation jar).
      Same reasoning as angus-mail above. Reviewed 2026-04-24.
    </notes>
    <packageUrl regex="true">^pkg:maven/org\.eclipse\.angus/jakarta\.mail@.*$</packageUrl>
    <cve>CVE-2025-7962</cve>
  </suppress>
  <!-- (C) Embedded POM entries that DC assigns CPE-only identifiers -->
  <suppress>
    <notes>
      CVE-2025-7962 — CPE cpe:eclipse:angus_mail (embedded angus-core POM
      inside angus-mail.jar; DC assigns CPE-only identifier to embedded POMs).
      Same reasoning: admin-controlled SMTP only. Reviewed 2026-04-24.
    </notes>
    <cpe regex="true">cpe:2\.3:a:eclipse:angus_mail:.*</cpe>
    <cve>CVE-2025-7962</cve>
  </suppress>
  <suppress>
    <notes>
      CVE-2025-7962 — CPE cpe:eclipse:jakarta_mail (embedded logging-mailhandler
      POM inside jakarta.mail.jar; CPE-only identifier on embedded POM).
      Same reasoning: admin-controlled SMTP only. Reviewed 2026-04-24.
    </notes>
    <cpe regex="true">cpe:2\.3:a:eclipse:jakarta_mail:.*</cpe>
    <cve>CVE-2025-7962</cve>
  </suppress>

  <suppress>
    <notes>
      CVE-2025-48924 — Apache Commons Lang 3.17.0.
      False positive CPE match — the CVE targets a different component.
      commons-lang3 is a utility library with no network-facing code.
      No fix available in 3.17.x at time of review. Reviewed 2026-04-23.
    </notes>
    <gav>org.apache.commons:commons-lang3:3.17.0</gav>
    <cve>CVE-2025-48924</cve>
  </suppress>

  <suppress>
    <notes>
      CVE-2026-0871 — Keycloak admin client 26.0.5.
      Server-side Keycloak vulnerability; the admin client library only
      makes REST API calls to the Keycloak server. Not exploitable via
      the client JAR. False positive CPE match. Reviewed 2026-04-23.
    </notes>
    <gav regex="true">^org\.keycloak:keycloak-admin-client:.*$</gav>
    <cve>CVE-2026-0871</cve>
  </suppress>

  <suppress>
    <notes>
      CVE-2025-68161 — log4j-api 2.24.3.
      False positive CPE match — log4j-api is a facade/API layer with
      no log4j-core on the classpath. The actual logging implementation
      is Logback (via SLF4J). log4j-api alone is not exploitable.
      Reviewed 2026-04-23.
    </notes>
    <gav>org.apache.logging.log4j:log4j-api:2.24.3</gav>
    <cve>CVE-2025-68161</cve>
  </suppress>

  <!--
    ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
    Netty 4.1.121.Final — multiple CVEs (CVSS 2.9–8.7)
    ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
    Netty is a transitive dependency via Reactor Netty (async HTTP client).
    These CVEs target Netty HTTP/2 and codec components. Spring Boot 3.5.0
    ships Netty 4.1.121.Final as its managed version; no newer version is
    available via the Spring BOM at time of review. Exposure is limited to
    internal async HTTP client usage only — no external inbound connections
    use raw Netty in the backend monolith.
    Using <packageUrl regex="true"> with @.*$ wildcard: canonical DC 12.x
    format; handles PURL qualifiers appended by DC normalisation.
    Reviewed 2026-04-24 by RazorMVP.
  -->
  <suppress>
    <notes>
      Netty 4.1.121.Final — CVE-2026-33871 (CVSS 8.7), CVE-2026-33870 (CVSS 7.5),
      CVE-2025-55163 (CVSS 8.2), CVE-2025-58056 (CVSS 2.9), CVE-2025-58057 (CVSS 6.9),
      CVE-2025-67735. Transitive dep; no inbound raw Netty connections in backend;
      no fix without Spring Boot BOM upgrade. Reviewed 2026-04-24.
    </notes>
    <packageUrl regex="true">^pkg:maven/io\.netty/netty-.*@.*$</packageUrl>
    <cve>CVE-2026-33871</cve>
    <cve>CVE-2026-33870</cve>
    <cve>CVE-2025-55163</cve>
    <cve>CVE-2025-58056</cve>
    <cve>CVE-2025-58057</cve>
    <cve>CVE-2025-67735</cve>
  </suppress>

